# M24.1 virtual-time slaving spike -- Renode's mainline Zynq UltraScale+ Cortex-R5 platform
# (docs/open-questions.md question 144), a trivial bare-loop firmware on rpu0 (the software
# under test does not matter -- this spike measures Renode's own time base). Renode's :name:/
# :description: script metadata fields must be single-line (confirmed against this build's
# own scripts/single-node/zynqmp_remoteproc.resc) -- the original multi-line :description:
# here failed to tokenize (recorded in REPORT.md), so the description moved to this comment.
:name: zynqmp-rpu-lockstep-spike

using sysbus
using sysbus.cluster0
using sysbus.cluster1

mach create "zynqmp-rpu-spike"

machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/zynqmp.repl

macro reset
"""
    cluster0 ForEach IsHalted true
    cluster1 ForEach IsHalted true
    rpu0 IsHalted false

    sysbus LoadBinary $ORIGIN/loop.bin 0x0 cpu=rpu0
    rpu0 PC 0x0
"""

runMacro $reset
